.TH BIGINTADDUINT_32 3 "2026-09-21" "BigNums" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigIntAddUInt_32, bigIntMulUInt_32, bigIntDivUInt32, bigIntModUInt32 \- perform scalar arithmetic on a big integer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqbignums.h\(dq
.sp
.BI "int bigIntAddUInt_32(BigInt *" "a" ", uint32_t " "b" ");"
.sp
.BI "int bigIntMulUInt_32(BigInt *" "a" ", uint32_t " "b" ");"
.sp
.BI "uint32_t bigIntDivUInt32(BigInt *" "a" ","
.BI "    uint32_t " "divisor" ");"
.sp
.BI "uint32_t bigIntModUInt32(const BigInt *" "a" ","
.BI "    uint32_t " "divisor" ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bigIntAddUInt_32()
adds b to a in place, extending the active limbs when needed.
Inactive limbs are ignored.
.B bigIntMulUInt_32()
multiplies a by b in place.  Multiplication by zero produces canonical zero.
.PP
.B bigIntDivUInt32()
replaces a with the quotient of a divided by divisor, discarding the fraction,
and returns the remainder.
.B bigIntModUInt32()
returns the same remainder without changing a.
A zero divisor leaves a unchanged.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Addition and multiplication return 0 on success or INT_MAX on capacity
overflow.  On overflow, a may already have been modified.
.PP
Division and modulo return a uint32_t remainder; they return INT_MAX when
divisor is zero.  Validate divisor before calling: INT_MAX can also be a
valid remainder when divisor is greater than INT_MAX.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bigIntMulFFT (3),
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
